+## scaleway_sd_configs
+
+Scaleway SD configuration {{% available_from "v1.133.0" %}} discovers scrape targets from [Scaleway](https://www.scaleway.com/en/) Instances.
+
+Configuration example:
+
+```yaml
+scrape_configs:
+- job_name: scaleway
+  scaleway_sd_configs:
+
+    # secret_key is the Scaleway API secret key to use for authentication (mandatory).
+    # It is sent to the API via the `X-Auth-Token` HTTP header.
+    # See: https://www.scaleway.com/en/docs/identity-and-access-management/iam/how-to/create-api-keys/
+  - secret_key: "..."
+
+    # project is the id of the Scaleway Project to discover instances from.
+    # Either project or organization must be set.
+    #
+    # project: "..."
+
+    # organization is the id of the Scaleway Organization to discover instances from.
+    # Either project or organization must be set.
+    #
+    # organization: "..."
+
+    # zone is the Scaleway zone to query for instances.
+    # See: https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/api/#regions-and-zones
+    #
+    # zone: "fr-par-1"
+
+    # port is an optional port to scrape metrics from.
+    # By default, port 80 is used.
+    #
+    # port: ...
+
+    # Additional HTTP API client options can be specified here.
+    # See https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/#http-api-client-options
+```
+
+Each discovered target has an [`__address__`](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/#how-to-modify-scrape-urls-in-targets) label set
+to `<ip>:<port>`, where `<ip>` is the public IPv4 address of the discovered instance (or its private IPv4 address if it has no public one), and `<port>`
+is the port from the `scaleway_sd_configs` (default port is `80`). Only instances in the `running` state are discovered.
+
+The following meta labels are available on discovered targets during [relabeling](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/):
+
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_arch`: the commercial architecture of the instance, such as `x86_64` or `arm64`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_hostname`: the hostname of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_id`: the unique ID of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_name`: the name of the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_organization_id`: the ID of the organization the instance belongs to.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_private_ipv4`: the private IPv4 address of the instance, if set.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_project_id`: the ID of the project the instance belongs to.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ipv4`: the public IPv4 address of the instance, if set.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_state`: the state of the instance, such as `running`, `stopped`, `starting` or `stopping`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_tags`: comma-separated list of tags applied to the instance.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_type`: the commercial type (plan) of the instance, such as `DEV1-S`.
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_zone`: the zone where the instance is located.
+
+The list of discovered Scaleway targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.scalewaySDCheckInterval` command-line flag, default: 30s.
+
 ## static_configs
 
 A static config allows specifying a list of targets and a common label set for them.
